        <briefdescription>
<para>Apply <computeroutput>mode</computeroutput> (CPOL/CPHA) and <computeroutput>midi_cycles</computeroutput> (<ref refid="classSoftChipSelectGuard_1acbe56b56922f2d3988c3ecf86208aa4a" kindref="member">CFG2.MIDI</ref>) to the HAL peripheral if they differ from the last applied values. Safe to call with SPE briefly cleared. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>midi_cycles</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>SCK idle cycles between data frames (0–15). See <ref refid="structhf__spi__device__config__t_1a4238394b7ed977bb267fad3ed3fefd56" kindref="member">hf_spi_device_config_t::inter_data_idle_cycles</ref> for why this is per-device: FIFO-serviced slaves want the pause, shift-register slaves (TLE92466ED) need a continuous 32-bit stream. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Caller must hold <ref refid="classStmSpiBusLock" kindref="compound">StmSpiBusLock</ref> and have every soft-CS idle (see <ref refid="classStmSpiBus_1ad2942f7f1b57611474e8839226685471" kindref="member">IdleAllChipSelects</ref>) — SPE toggle must not clock a selected slave. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
